==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|head=[[come]] [[across]]|comes across|coming across|came across|come across}}

# {{label|en|idiomatic}} To give an [[appearance]] or [[impression]]; to project a certain [[image]].
#: ''A business suit and briefcase help her to '''come across''' as the competent professional she is.''
# To [[find]], usually by [[accident]].
#: ''In the meadow he will '''come across''' a rare flower.''

